///1PIP
Help by Willem Aandewiel
PIP - Copy files and concatenate text

///2SYNTAX
PIP destination=source
The destination is on the left; the source is on the right.

  E>A:PIP E:COPY.TXT=A:WELCOME.TXT
  E>A:PIP E:=A:*.HLP

The second command copies matching .HLP files to E:.

///2VERIFYING
  E>A:PIP E:=A:HELP.COM[V]

[V] verifies the copy by reading the written data again.
Existing destination files may be replaced.
Check the destination and source before issuing a command.

///2BINARY
  E>A:PIP E:=A:OLD.HLP[OV]

[O] treats the source as binary data rather than stopping at 1AH.
Use this for original indexed HLP files: their index may contain
an embedded 1AH byte. [V] adds copy verification.
PIP already treats .COM files as binary files.

///2TEXT
  E>A:PIP NEW.TXT=PART1.TXT,PART2.TXT

Concatenates the text sources in the specified order.
Do not use concatenation to link two executable programs.
PIP without arguments displays its own * prompt.
An empty line at that prompt exits PIP.
